        "original_id": "92dd236c-32b8-58f8-bbc1-f6b3a66001f1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Mack Brown\n- Organizations: Texas Longhorns, Iowa State Cyclones, Kansas State Wildcats, Baylor Bears, Eastern Kentucky, Kent State, Miami, ESPN\n- Places: Darrell K Royal–Texas Memorial Stadium, Manhattan, Kansas\n- Events: 2011 Texas Longhorns football team season, 2011 Iowa State Cyclones football team season, 2011 Kansas State Wildcats football team season, Farmageddon\n- Roles: head coach, college football commentator\n\nFacts:\n- In 2011, the Texas Longhorns football team was led by head coach Mack Brown in his 14th year and played its home games at Darrell K Royal–Texas Memorial Stadium.\n- In 2011, the Iowa State Cyclones began conference play with a home loss to the Texas Longhorns and ended conference play with a loss at Kansas State in Manhattan, Kansas in the Farmageddon series, finishing conference play with a 3–6 record.\n- In 2011, the Kansas State Wildcats won all three non-conference games against Eastern Kentucky, Kent State, and Miami.\n- In 2011, the Kansas State Wildcats opened conference play with a close home victory over the Baylor Bears and ended it with a victory over rival Iowa State in the Farmageddon showdown.\n- Mack Brown is currently a college football commentator for ESPN.",
